<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Trans Hex lifts interim shr, div increased.</title>
<headline>Trans Hex lifts interim shr, div increased.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended 30 September</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, attrib (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre abnormal items     180.0	 vs    133.5</p>
<p>    - post abnormal items    180.0	 vs    125.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     40.0	 vs    34.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			39.19	 vs    34.57</p>
<p>    Tax			    14.50	 vs    14.45</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 0.21	 vs    0.76</p>
<p>Turnover</p>
<p>    - diamonds		  102.56	vs     87.69</p>
<p>    - lime			 16.93	vs     14.74</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		 nil	vs     1.21 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Trans Hex Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said 25.98 million rand worth of sales at a unit of the lime division, which was sold during the first half of last year, was not included in the turnover figure.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
